    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1040">

                <pb facs="0964" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg650"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-30T17:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your December 29, 10 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi>. As
                    circumstances of case appear to show that register was fraudulently obtained,
                    Department of Commerce requests that Consul withhold ship’s papers and refuse to
                    discharge crew until further notice. Consul instructed in this sense. Department
                    of Commerce would be pleased to see vessel and crew interned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
